The paper proposes Uni-RAG, a multi-modal retrieval-augmented generation pipeline. It retrieves multi-modal educational materials (text-image, with varied query styles such as sketches and art) and generates text explanations, and it reports experiments on multi-modal benchmarks. E9 excludes multimodal-only RAG, and this one appears to be multimodal-only, since retrieval is over text-image content with style-conditioned queries. The generator is a compact language model, so it may take retrieved text, but the title and abstract emphasize multi-modal retrieval throughout, which fits E9.

Some ambiguity remains: the retrieved materials could include text, and the generator is an instruction-tuned language model rather than a vision-language model. Even so, "multi-modal benchmarks" and "multi-modal retrieval module" point to multimodal RAG, so I lean toward E9.

{"decision": "EXCLUDE", "code": "E9", "reason": "Multi-modal (text-image, style-varied queries) retrieval-augmented pipeline; multimodal-only RAG is out of scope."}
